kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[6]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,tt01,"five-layer-test-architecture","The TUI test harness MUST be organized as five non-overlapping layers: layer 1 key-sequence-to-state assertions (drive Component::handle_input with byte sequences and assert on model state modeled on helix test_key_sequence); layer 2 insta snapshot golden (assert whole-screen viewport output via assert_snapshot!); layer 3 timing infrastructure (injectable Clock trait for synchronous logic like paste-burst and tokio start_paused for async logic like debounce); layer 4 proptest state-machine (random key sequences plus invariant assertions for editor state machines); layer 5 end-to-end terminal integration (portable-pty as primary driver plus tmux smoke for real-terminal compatibility). Each layer MUST have a distinct non-overlapping responsibility: layers 1-4 run in-process via the existing VirtualTerminal cell-grid oracle; layer 5 spawns the real binary.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tt02,"key-sequence-helper","The TUI test support MUST provide a generic key-sequence driver that accepts a byte string of terminal input, dispatches it through Component::handle_input, and exposes state assertions (assert_text, assert_cursor, assert_screen_contains). The MutableComponent pattern (Rc<RefCell> injected as Component) MUST be generalized from its current single-test-local definition into tests/support/ so any test can mount a widget, drive keys, and assert across multiple frames without hand-wiring Rc/RefCell per test. Tests MUST NOT rebuild a second TUI instance to observe a second frame (the current workaround documented in virtual_terminal_test.rs:178-184); the helper MUST mutate the same instance in place.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tt03,"insta-snapshot-golden","The TUI test harness MUST use insta (assert_snapshot!) for whole-screen render regression: the VirtualTerminal::viewport() output (or a human-readable rendering of the cell grid) is fed to assert_snapshot!, snapshots are reviewed via cargo insta review, and changes to layout/colors/wrapping surface as diffs. Structural assertions (exact cell content, specific SGR style on a cell) MUST continue to use explicit assert_eq for precision. The two assertion styles MUST coexist (snapshot for regression breadth, assert_eq for pinpoint correctness).",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tt04,"timing-injectable-clock","Timing-dependent TUI logic (paste-burst detection, autocomplete debounce, loader spinner frame scheduling) MUST be testable deterministically without real wall-clock sleeps. Synchronous timing logic MUST accept an injected Clock trait (now() returns a controllable Instant) so tests advance time step-by-step; async timing logic MUST be tested under #[tokio::test(start_paused = true)] with tokio::time::advance. Tests MUST NOT use thread::sleep or std::thread::sleep to wait for timing effects (flaky by construction). The paste-burst window boundary (just-inside vs just-outside the 8ms inter-char or 120ms enter-suppress window) MUST be explicitly covered.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tt05,"portable-pty-e2e-primary","End-to-end TUI tests MUST use portable-pty as the primary integration driver: spawn the real binary as a PTY child, inject key sequences via the writer handle (with explicit sleep between keys when timing matters), read the raw byte stream from the reader handle, feed it to the existing VirtualTerminal (vte-based cell-grid parser), and assert on the resulting grid (cell content, SGR styles, cursor position). This layer MUST cover crossterm's real event parsing of multi-byte sequences (Ctrl+arrow, Alt+arrow, bracketed paste markers) that cannot be exercised through in-process handle_input alone. portable-pty tests live in the workspace-level tests/tui_e2e/ directory (not packages/xylitol-tui/tests/) because they test the assembled binary, not the crate.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tt06,"tmux-real-terminal-smoke","The TUI test harness MUST include a small set (3-5 cases) of real-terminal smoke tests driven by tmux (via a hand-written thin wrapper using std::process::Command, NOT a tmux binding crate): create a detached session (tmux new-session -d -s <name> -x <w> -y <h>), inject keys via tmux send-keys (supporting C-Left/M-Right/Escape/Enter special keys), capture the screen via tmux capture-pane -e -p (preserving SGR escape sequences), and assert via string containment plus insta snapshot (with filters to mask volatile parts). tmux tests MUST be marked #[ignore] and run via a dedicated justfile target (test-tui-e2e), NOT in the main test matrix, because they are slow (1-3s per case) and depend on a real tmux binary plus TERM=xterm-256color. A render-ready signal (env XYLITOL_TEST_RENDER_SIGNAL=1 writing RENDER_DONE <frame_id> to stderr) MAY be added to reduce capture flakiness if screen-content polling proves unreliable.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[6]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tt01,five-layers-distinct,"the test directory layout is inspected","tests/support/ contains key-sequence helpers, snapshot fixtures, a Clock abstraction; tests/tui_e2e/ contains portable-pty and tmux drivers","the five layers are present and each has a non-overlapping responsibility (no layer duplicates another layer's assertions)"
  tt02,keys-helper-drives-editor,"a test mounts an Input component via the generalized helper and calls keys on an abc-then-left-then-backspace sequence","the key sequence is dispatched through handle_input","the component state reflects ab (typed abc, left-arrow moved cursor, backspace deleted b) without rebuilding a second instance"
  tt03,snapshot-detects-layout-regression,"a TUI component render output changes layout (e.g. panel border style)","the test runs and cargo insta review is invoked","the snapshot diff surfaces the layout change for human review"
  tt04,paste-burst-window-boundary,"a paste-burst detector with an 8ms inter-char threshold is tested with mock clock","two chars injected 7ms apart then 9ms apart","the 7ms pair is detected as a burst (enter suppressed) and the 9ms pair is not (enter submits), deterministically without thread::sleep"
  tt05,ctrl-arrow-parsed-via-pty,"the assembled xylitol binary is spawned under portable-pty and the byte sequence for Ctrl+Left is written to the PTY","crossterm reads and parses the event","the editor cursor jumps by one word left (verified via the cell-grid assertion on the fed-back output)"
  tt06,tmux-captures-colored-screen,"the xylitol binary runs in a tmux session with TERM=xterm-256color and a reply containing a red-colored word is rendered","tmux capture-pane -e -p is called","the captured output contains the SGR red-color escape sequence (CSI 31 m or equivalent) confirming color rendering works in a real terminal"
